Recommended path for you
-----------------------------
Now:Feign with URL → quick working(@FeignClient(name = "product-service", url = "http://localhost:8104"))
Next: Add LoadBalancer dependency
Later: Add Eureka → remove URLs → use lb:// (Production ready so i choose this one)

Without Loadbalancer settings in ApiGateway
------------------------------------------
cloud:
    gateway:
      server:
        webflux:
          routes:
            - id: user-service
              uri: http://localhost:8103
              predicates:
                - Path=/api/users/**

With LoadBalancer settings in ApiGateway
------------------------------------------
spring:
  cloud:
    gateway:
      server:
        webflux:
          routes:
            - id: user-service
              uri: lb://user-service
              predicates:
                - Path=/api/users/**
REsillence
=============
resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.productService.failure-rate-threshold=50
resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.productService.sliding-window-size=5
resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.productService.wait-duration-in-open-state=10s
resilience4j.circuitbreaker.instances.productService.permitted-number-of-calls-in-half-open-state=2                

failure-rate-threshold=50
-----------------------------
If 50% of calls fail → circuit opens
Example:
Total calls = 10
Failed calls = 5
5/10 = 50% → Circuit opens

sliding-window-size=5
---------------------------
👉 How many recent calls to consider: Only last 5 calls are checked
Example:
Last 5 calls result: ✔ ❌ ❌ ✔ ❌
Failures = 3/5 = 60%
👉 Above 50% → Circuit opens

wait-duration-in-open-state=10s
-------------------------------
👉 How long circuit stays OPEN: Circuit stays OPEN for 10 seconds
During this time: Cart → Product call ❌ blocked → fallback method called directly

permitted-number-of-calls-in-half-open-state=2
------------------------------------------------
👉 After 10 seconds, circuit goes to HALF-OPEN
Allow only 2 test calls
Case:
✔ If both succeed: Circuit CLOSES (normal again)
❌ If any fails: Circuit OPENS again             
   
